  "body": "Part of #290 (design decisions D1-D10 in its research comment).\n\nDepends on: #534.\n\nOff by default (D6). When on, tab count, width and position are required, with no invented default. The main cut leaves the tabs; a later cut-off pass removes them. Slug analysis from the wire verify sub-issue refuses an unsupported slug unless tabs or a capture are set.\n\n**Done means:** a die with two tabs leaves the slug held until the cut-off pass, and the same cut with tabs off and no capture is refused by name.",
